    "writing.howto.word-order": "Tap the words in the right order — they move into the line. Tap a word in the line to send it back. English word order is fixed, so the order itself carries the meaning.",
    "writing.howto.transform": "Read the sentence and the instruction next to it. Write your own version: same meaning, different form. The model answer appears after you check.",
    "writing.howto.connectors": "The linking words are in the bank at the top. Tap a linking word, then tap the gap — or drag it with the mouse. Each word is used once.",
    "writing.howto.punctuation": "Rewrite the sentence with capital letters and punctuation. Do not change the words themselves.",
    "writing.howto.expand": "Turn the notes into a full sentence: add articles, prepositions and the right verb form. Keep the meaning.",
    "writing.howto.register": "The same idea, two versions. Choose the one that fits the reader. Register is not about being polite — it is about distance.",
    "writing.howto.idea-bank": "Sort the ideas into two columns: what goes into your text and what only waters it down. Then choose the three strongest ideas.",
    "writing.howto.outline-builder": "Put the blocks into the four parts of the text. The checker knows the logic of the genre: some blocks cannot stand where you put them.",
    "writing.howto.guided-write": "Answer one question at a time, in English, one or two sentences. At the end your answers become a draft in the Writing Pad. The hints are questions, not ready sentences: the text stays yours.",
    "writing.howto.free-write": "Now the whole text, on your own. The Writing Pad gives you the checklist, the phrase bank, the linking words and your plan. The timer is optional.",
    "writing.howto.overall": "This is the site's own summary of the genre. It counts the exercises you have finished, how accurate you were, and the scores of the text you submitted, and turns all of that into one band. Nothing here is a school grade — it only shows what to work on next.",
